Hermes Portable: venv stamp ignores the lock's download source.

Hermes Portable switches uv.lock between PyPI and a mirror (Nexus) by
rewriting only `registry = ...` / `url = ...` values (hp_sources.py); package
names, versions and hashes are unchanged, so the environment built from
either lock is identical. _uv_lock_digest() now hashes the lock with
url/registry/upload-time/size values and exclude-newer options removed, so
switching sources does not invalidate the sealed payload venv (no full
re-sync after `hermes-portable sources pypi use-nexus`).

diff --git a/pm/packages.py b/pm/packages.py
